      en: "Wat Chetuphon is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Thailand. A temple in Sukhothai Historical Park known for its four large Buddha statues in different postures: walking, standing, sitting, and reclining. Located south of the walled city. The statues symbolize the four postures of Buddha. Surrounded by a moat. This site holds particular significance in the history of Thailand, from the Sukhothai and Ayutthaya kingdoms to modern Bangkok. Like many notable places in Thailand, it combines regional character with the legacy of the Chao Phraya, the Mekong and Buddhist tradition. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Thailand, between the Andaman coast, rice paddies and tropical forests.",
