      en: ["A former royal palace in Bangkok, believed to be the world's largest teakwood building. Built in 1900 by King Chulalongkorn (Rama V).", "Located within the Kingdom of Thailand.", "Shaped by the monsoon climate of Southeast Asia.", "Linked to the heritage of the Sukhothai and Ayutthaya kingdoms."],
